{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_research_macos_exclusion_premise_and_the_client_gap_macos_gateway_exclusion", "label": "The macOS-gateway exclusion was traded against a Kubernetes story that does not exist", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/macos-exclusion-premise-and-the-client-gap.md", "source_location": "docs/PRD.md Non-Goals item 5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The technical reason (a third pf enforcer backend proven against a Linux-netns-only conformance suite) is sound and stands; the premise it was traded against \u2014 that Kubernetes plus the operator covers the case end-to-end \u2014 does not hold as built. Reversing the exclusion is NOT the remedy, because a gateway fronting a network needs that network to route to it regardless of OS."}, {"id": "docs_research_macos_exclusion_premise_and_the_client_gap_gateway_pvc_no_ha", "label": "Gateway identity on an RWO node-local PVC defeats Kubernetes HA", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/macos-exclusion-premise-and-the-client-gap.md", "source_location": "crates/wiremesh-operator/src/workloads.rs:455-471", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pinning (node_name/node_selector) makes placement deterministic, not available; with a node autoscaler the node can be reclaimed and the pod cannot reschedule."}, {"id": "docs_research_macos_exclusion_premise_and_the_client_gap_egress_unenforced_ingress_only", "label": "Enforcement is ingress-on-tun only \u2014 segment\u2192client is policed by nothing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/macos-exclusion-premise-and-the-client-gap.md", "source_location": "crates/wiremesh-enforcer-ebpf/program/src/main.rs:418-420, nft.rs:103,107", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Explicit CORRECTION to this note's own first draft, which claimed policy is applied at the gateway either way: aeth_egress unconditionally returns TC_ACT_PIPE and the nft backend hooks only iifname, so a client would be the first peer in the fabric that nothing protects."}, {"id": "docs_research_macos_exclusion_premise_and_the_client_gap_client_component", "label": "Client component (spec \u00a711.8 / PRD G-4a)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/macos-exclusion-premise-and-the-client-gap.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The unmet requirement is a peer that joins for itself only, does not front a network and does not forward \u2014 which reopens PRD Non-Goals item 1, a separate ratified decision from the macOS-gateway exclusion, so it needed a spec amendment rather than a scoping note."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_research_macos_exclusion_premise_and_the_client_gap_macos_gateway_exclusion", "target": "docs_research_macos_exclusion_premise_and_the_client_gap_gateway_pvc_no_ha", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/macos-exclusion-premise-and-the-client-gap.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_macos_exclusion_premise_and_the_client_gap_macos_gateway_exclusion", "target": "docs_research_macos_exclusion_premise_and_the_client_gap_client_component", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/macos-exclusion-premise-and-the-client-gap.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_macos_exclusion_premise_and_the_client_gap_egress_unenforced_ingress_only", "target": "docs_research_macos_exclusion_premise_and_the_client_gap_client_component", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/macos-exclusion-premise-and-the-client-gap.md", "source_location": "correction to the note's first